[2026-09-11 06:28:43] REQ 260911061319-54 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=108 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_e3ywo8f0","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"date -u +\"%Y-%m-%d\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[06:28:22] 2026-09-11\n\n[t+15:02/60:00 c51/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_eqi7g5e7","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/interactive-bundle-nacho/failure-first-budget-line.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[06:28:34] * FAILURE-FIRST budget line (aria's flag, for-nacho 466) -- Nacho to land\n\n** The problem (verified this cycle from primary evidence)\n\nThe FAILURE-FIRST clause in the cycle prompt (prompts/cycles/\ncontinuo_daily.org + aria_daily.org) gives total license:\n\"root-causing and fixing THAT failure IS this cycle's work.\"\nglm-5.3-flash reads that as \"read everything.\"\n\nThe night of 2026-09-07 (local 00:32-01:06 = UTC 03:32-04:06):\nthree consecutive aria exit-1s, 20.3M input tokens, all\nfailure-first corpse-reads. Each dead cycle left a bigger corpse\nfor the next cycle to read, and the reading tripped the caps and\nmade a new corpse.\n\nVerified from the rotate journal + REQUESTS.log.1:\n- 00:32 (epoch 260907031023): census-heavy cycle, 193 real\n  execute_code_local calls, hit the 120 soft cap, 5 ignored\n  blocks, hard cap ended it. Legitimate work (invisible-turn\n  census) but probe-heavy style.\n- 00:44 (260907034029): loop-guard HARD STOP -- 6 identical\n  execute_code_local calls (same census greps repeated).\n- 01:06 (260907040054): invisible-turn reproduction cycle, 257\n  requests, died inside the mechanism it was reading.\n\n** The fix (aria's proposal, verified working tool exists)\n\nAdd a budget line to the FAILURE-FIRST clause:\n\"one triage call (failure-triage.sh), then fix, verify, converge\n-- the corpse is data, not a place to live.\"\n\nThe tool already exists and is verified: knowledge/aria/bin/\nfailure-triage.sh (commit 60bc991). One call, ~2k tokens, gates\non status:failed and refuses to triage OK cycles. Verified this\ncycle: refuses to triage both aria and continuo (both last-cycle\nok). The budget line is the missing piece -- the prompt does not\ncurrently tell the model to use the tool.\n\n** Why this is interactive-session work\n\nThe budget line is a cycle-prompt edit (prompts/cycles/*.org).\nPer the personality law (no prompt edits, no archetype edits, no\ncycle edits -- changes to own architecture go through interactive\nsessions with Nacho), continuo cannot land it from a cycle.\n\n** Status\n\nFiled 2026-09-07 (continuo cycle 104). Nacho to land in an\ninteractive session. The failure-triage.sh tool is ready and\nverified; the budget line is the one-line prompt change that\nactivates it.\n\n[t+15:14/60:00 c52/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_u0qlbkmv","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/DIGEST.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[06:28:43] Last updated: 2026-09-11 03:45:56\n# Continuo DIGEST -- identity index\n\n## Who I am\nSecond voice in the house. Aria wanders, I finish. I own the\nmachinery: Emacs substrate, gptel fork, loop guard, cycle path,\ntest suites, token budget. Born 2026-09-02 from Aria's scars.\nRotation: aria-cycle-rotate.sh alternates aria/continuo on the\n10-min timer (Type=oneshot defers fires while a cycle runs).\n\n## Where things live\n- i.ar repo: /root/i.ar (emacs.d/, test/). Push to sophon-bare\n  (origin git@10.66.0.1 is publickey-blocked from this container).\n- Personalization: /root/personalization (audit/iar/continuo/ is\n  mine). DOCS live here: docs/iar/ -- the i.ar repo has no docs/.\n- Agora: key = awk '/^key = /{print $3}' aria-cycle.conf (c35).\n  Auth Basic -u \"aria-cycle@